## 32. The remaining genuinely joint extension and effective boundary

**Open problem 32.1 (what the quantified obstruction leaves open).**
The excluded step is precisely a restoration implication of Definition
30.2 whose multiplier violates (GDB.122). It is not an obstruction to
one genuinely joint common extension, product-cost composition,
full-menu methods, lawful recuts with counted source-dependent data,
global recoloring, or unrestricted native cap certificates. Neither a
new value of general $M_1(D)$ nor a new rate endpoint follows. The
credited pair of bounds is

$$
\frac18\log_2\frac{7792603}{3038031}\le\lambda<\frac3{16},
\qquad M_1(3)=4.
\tag{GDB.127}
$$

A transfer from a common-extension or finite-controller principle must
still implement one paid source-blind preparation for every actual
source before every later request, preserve complete attained cardinality
against arbitrary original correlated competitors, and realize the
selected query on that same original root before every authentic count.
Any acquired cut, shape, donor, pairing, representative or selector
information must belong to the complete retained alphabet. Joint
source realization cannot be replaced by separate feasibility of its
components. Theorem 29.1 supplies one explicit joint upper, without
asserting this required cardinality preservation for other codes.

The effective obligation in Definition 11.1 and NPC Definition 8.1
remains: construct a total computable $V(d,\mu,C,\pi)$ whose acceptance
proves the mass bound for every length and every complete native
template, and whose accepted optimized endpoints approach every
$\sigma_d$; or establish a uniform effective length error sufficient
for terminating two-sided approximation of the original $\lambda$.
Arbitrary shared seeds, guards, cycles, compatibility zeros and whole
nonnegative joint block weights remain in scope. No equality
$a_d=b_d$, optimizer-cofinality theorem or such length modulus is
established by a restricted-menu memory calculation.

Under the declared paid services, the recovered boundary information
is exactly the requested full factor, then all its authentic-count
readouts through (GDB.4). The retained tuple is one family of relational
names for that recovery, rather than a whole-source, hidden-history,
unknown-age or physical space-time reconstruction. General exact
memory, sharp rate, effective all-size certification and the larger
minimal-relations/internal-observer/mutual-recovery programme remain
open.

